          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "BIERTON AND BROUGHTON SP 81 SE                                          GRAND UNION CANAL                                                   AYLESBURY ARM 5/353                                             BRIDGE NO 12 II                                                GV Bridge over canal. 1811-13; Engineer Henry Provis for Grand Junction Canal Company; some late C20 patching. Red brick, mostly in English bond. Round arch with number plate over and base-stones on north (boat) side (to prevent damage to brickwork). Raised brick band below parapet which has rounded brick coping and end stones. Square projecting end - piers on stepped, battered, plinths terminate outswept ends of parapet. The bridge carried a farm track over the canal and has been little altered since the Aylesbury Arm opened in 1815. Listing NGR: SP8556214150"
    }
